Step 1: First leg  
\[
\text{Time}=\frac{84\text{ km}}{60\text{ km/h}}=1.4\text{ h}
\]
\[
0.4\text{ h}=0.4\times 60=24\text{ min}
\]
So the first leg takes **1 hour 24 minutes**.

Step 2: Add stop time  
Stop = **12 minutes**.

Step 3: Second leg  
\[
\text{Time}=\frac{45\text{ km}}{90\text{ km/h}}=0.5\text{ h}=30\text{ min}
\]

Step 4: Total time  
\[
1\text{ h }24\text{ min}+12\text{ min}+30\text{ min}
\]
\[
24+12+30=66\text{ min}=1\text{ h }6\text{ min}
\]
\[
1\text{ h}+1\text{ h }6\text{ min}=2\text{ h }6\text{ min}
\]

Step 5: Add to departure time  
Departure: **9:10**  
\[
9:10+2\text{ h }6\text{ min}=11:16
\]

The train arrives at **11:16**.
